TEST MATERIAL of paper-one-port (P3), never a secret. The self-signed test certificate, CN and SAN oneport.test, valid 2026-10-02 to 2126-09-08.
It exists only for the test suite and the lab's loopback runs (hypotheses.md, section 2.1;
design/proposal.md, I24: "one ECDSA P-256 certificate, made from a fixed test key in the
repository's test fixtures"). Anyone may read it; nothing outside this repository trusts it.
Made on L on 2026-10-02 with the pinned OpenSSL 3.5.9 (release flavour, bench/third_party):
  openssl genpkey -algorithm EC -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -pkeyopt ec_param_enc:named_curve -out test-key.pem
  openssl req -x509 -new -key test-key.pem -sha256 -days 36500 -config req.cnf -out test-cert.pem
req.cnf: CN oneport.test; subjectAltName DNS:oneport.test; basicConstraints critical CA:FALSE;
keyUsage critical digitalSignature; extendedKeyUsage serverAuth; subjectKeyIdentifier hash.
PEM readers skip these lines before the BEGIN line.
